--TEST--
A Core\IO::move the operating system refuses throws an IOError naming both ends of the attempt and leaves the source exactly where it was — over a destination directory that is not there and a source that is not there — spec § 14, `rule:security/capability-check-at-the-door`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The two ways a granted move fails, and one claim about each: nothing is lost,
// and the message says which pair of paths it was about. A two-path member that
// named one end would send half of the readers of this message to the wrong
// file, which is why the door builds the `from -> to` spelling. Each end is a
// literal, so the door names it resolved from this file's folder, and
// `Here::path` resolves the expected text the same way.
class Here {
    public static function path(#[Core\Path] string $path): string {
        return $path;
    }
}
Core\IO::write("present.txt", "kept");

int $refusals = 0;
int $namingBothEnds = 0;

// A destination whose directory does not exist. The capability covers it --
// the grant is this whole tree -- so what refuses is the filesystem.
try {
    Core\IO::move("present.txt", "no-such-dir/present.txt");
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (IOError $failed) {
    $refusals = $refusals + 1;
    if (Core\Str::contains($failed->message, Here::path("present.txt") . " -> " . Here::path("no-such-dir/present.txt"))) {
        $namingBothEnds = $namingBothEnds + 1;
    }
}

// A source that is not there. The same member, the same capability, a different
// end at fault -- and the message has to be able to say so.
try {
    Core\IO::move("absent.txt", "wherever.txt");
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (IOError $failed) {
    $refusals = $refusals + 1;
    if (Core\Str::contains($failed->message, Here::path("absent.txt") . " -> " . Here::path("wherever.txt"))) {
        $namingBothEnds = $namingBothEnds + 1;
    }
}

echo "attempts: 2, refused: ", $refusals as string,
     ", naming both ends: ", $namingBothEnds as string, "\n";

// Nothing was lost and nothing was created: a failed move is not a move that
// got half way.
if (Core\IO::read("present.txt") == "kept") {
    echo "the source is where it was, holding what it held\n";
} else {
    echo "the source did not survive\n";
}
if (Core\IO::exists("wherever.txt")) {
    echo "a destination was created anyway\n";
} else {
    echo "no destination was created\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
write = ["."]
--EXPECT--
attempts: 2, refused: 2, naming both ends: 2
the source is where it was, holding what it held
no destination was created
